message: "If you use this project, please cite it as below."
title: "German AI Text Detector: Distinguishing Human-Written, AI-Generated and AI-Assisted German Text"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hijazi
    given-names: Hassan
  - family-names: Issa
    given-names: Ali
repository-code: "https://github.com/HassanHijaze/german-ai-text-detector-from-scratch"
url: "https://huggingface.co/HassanHijazi"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-06
keywords:
  - AI text detection
  - AI-assisted writing
  - German
  - natural language processing
  - text classification
  - transformers
abstract: >-
  A three-class machine learning project that classifies German text as
  human-written, AI-generated, or AI-assisted (human text rewritten by a
  language model). It compares six supervised models and a zero-shot LLM
  baseline on 30,629 German academic texts, evaluates generalization on
  out-of-distribution data, and provides a Docker web app for the detector.